<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Momentum Life half year earnings leap.</title>
<headline>Momentum Life half year earnings leap.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)			60.6     vs 34.6</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)			  62.0     vs 34.6</p>
<p>    Div, notional (cts)			26.0     vs 18.5</p>
<p>    Premium income			     1,974.3  vs 1,183.2</p>
<p>    Attrib net taxed surplus		 83.5     vs 46.6</p>
<p>Contributions by business area:</p>
<p>     Life insurance/asset management     38.2     vs 26.0</p>
<p>     Health insurance			   2.9     vs  1.4</p>
<p>     Banking activities			36.0     vs 26.7</p>
<p>     Short-term insurance		     6.4     vs  7.5 loss</p>
<p>Funds under management		   42.5     vs 32.2</p>
<p>Full name: Momentum Life Assurers Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Momentum said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the dividend. It is also proposing to sub-divide the shares on the basis of 10 shares per each share presently in issue.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
